summary:
- topic: Superintendent Transition
  text: The Board approved a separation agreement for Superintendent Matheney, effective
    August 8, 2025. George Entwistle was appointed as the interim superintendent for
    the 2025-2026 school year, with the board expressing confidence in his experience
    and leadership.
- topic: Board Leadership Election
  text: Tandy Ratliff was unanimously elected as the new Board Chair, with board members
    highlighting her temperament, experience in special education and DEI issues,
    and courageous leadership during a period of district transition.
- topic: District Operations and Facilities Updates
  text: Updates included the successful launch of summer meal and extended school
    year programs, progress on elementary school security upgrades (surveillance cameras,
    secure vestibules, roofing), and a 'Fill the Backpack Day' initiative with the
    Maine Mall. Kindergarten enrollment is ongoing, with a target of 200 students.
- topic: AI in Education Strategy
  text: The Director of Technology, Andy Wallace, presented the AI Steering Committee's
    work, including a position statement, student handbook wording, and staff training
    on the approved 'Magic School AI' tool. Future plans include student AI education
    across all grade levels and a 'traffic light' protocol for AI usage in assignments.
- topic: Financial and Committee Reports
  text: The Finance Committee reported a preliminary deficit for FY24-25 in school
    administration, program function, and transportation, prompting further review.
    The Buildings and Grounds Committee provided an encouraging update on the South
    Portland Middle School athletic field's recovery and ongoing safety assessments.
- topic: Superintendent's Farewell Remarks
  text: Superintendent Matheney delivered his final report, reflecting on district
    achievements such as improved SAT scores and reduced chronic absenteeism. He also
    addressed significant challenges, including potential federal funding cuts, gun
    violence, and the transformative impact of AI on education and society.
- topic: Community Engagement
  text: A teacher invited the board and community to the Maine Construction Academy
    graduation, showcasing student projects. The meeting also included public comment
    periods for agenda items and general school-related matters.
